# GD-24 (round 19, writer 10): settled; was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.4. L §2.4: "a span with no start, a row governing always among them, then by start": the always row first.
# The old comment:
# L §2.4 sorts version items "then by the start of their own governs span or their instant (a row with no span of its
# own first, then a span with no start)"; `governs always` is no span of the grammar (rowmeta: "governs" (lspan |
# "always"), L §2.2), so where a row governing always sorts among rows of one target and keys with spans is not stated:
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED (it decides the canonical text, so the hash).
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

input y: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  y = 1 governs 2027..
  replace y = 2 governs always
=== expect
